---
import Layout from '../../components/Layout.astro';
import Matcher from '../../components/Matcher.astro';
---

<Layout
	path="/tools/logo-font-identifier"
	title="Logo Font Identifier — Find the Font Used in a Logo"
	description="Identify the typeface behind a logo or wordmark. Free logo font identifier that names the font — and suggests free alternatives when the original is custom or commercial."
	canonical="/tools/logo-font-identifier"
>
	<section class="container-page py-12 sm:py-16">
		<p class="eyebrow">Tools</p>
		<h1 class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-display-lg font-semibold tracking-tight">
			Logo font identifier
		</h1>
		<p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-body-lg text-body">
			Crop a wordmark down to its letters and this tool names the closest typeface — with a free
			lookalike whenever the original was drawn or licensed commercially.
		</p>

		<div class="mx-auto mt-8 max-w-3xl text-left">
			<Matcher />
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="container-page pb-16 sm:pb-24">
		<div class="max-w-3xl">
			<h2 class="text-display-md font-semibold tracking-tight">How to identify a logo font</h2>
			<ol class="mt-4 list-decimal space-y-2 pl-6 text-body-md text-body">
				<li>Find the highest-resolution version of the logo you can — an SVG export or press kit beats a screenshot.</li>
				<li>Crop to just the lettering, excluding icons, taglines and registered marks.</li>
				<li>Fix any misread letters in the editor before matching.</li>
			</ol>

			<h2 class="mt-10 text-display-md font-semibold tracking-tight">What to expect from logo lettering</h2>
			<ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-body-md text-body">
				<li>Many logos are <strong>drawn artwork, not typeset text</strong> — expect a close relative rather than an exact name, which is still enough to recreate the look.</li>
				<li>All-caps wordmarks carry less identifying detail than lowercase; results lean toward “similar” rather than “strong”.</li>
				<li>If the match is a commercial face like Helvetica or Gotham, every result includes a free alternative such as Inter or Montserrat.</li>
				<li>Straight-on, unrotated crops always beat perspective shots of signage.</li>
			</ul>

			<p class="mt-8 text-body-md text-body">
				Once identified, open any match’s detail page for a specimen, download link and copy-paste
				CSS. Your image stays on your device — matching runs entirely in your browser.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>
